The logic for iterating over attributes and checking for specific metadata attributes can be improved for clarity. The use of a `while` loop with a flag (`keepIterating`) to control the iteration is not as clear as using a simple `for-each` loop or breaking out of the loop when conditions are met.
In `#YJM1Z`, consider:
```java
for (Attribute attr : plan.output()) {
    if (attr instanceof MetadataAttribute ma) {
        if (ma.name().equals(MetadataAttribute.SCORE)) {
            score = attr;
        } else if (isTimeSeries) {
            if (ma.name().equals(MetadataAttribute.TSID_FIELD)) {
                tsid = attr;
            } else if (ma.name().equals(MetadataAttribute.TIMESTAMP_FIELD)) {
                timestamp = attr;
            }
        }
    }
    if (score != null && (!isTimeSeries || (tsid != null && timestamp != null))) {
        break;
    }
}
```
In `#GZRG9`, the logic for checking scoring attributes is correct but can be simplified. The use of a flag (`hasScoring`) and nested loops can be streamlined.
```java
if (filter != null) {
    boolean hasScoring = false;
    physicalPlan.forEachDown(EsQueryExec.class, esQueryExec -> {
        if (!hasScoring && esQueryExec.hasScoring()) {
            hasScoring = true;
        }
    });
    if (!hasScoring) {
        physicalPlan.forEachDown(FragmentExec.class, fragmentExec -> {
            fragmentExec.fragment().forEachDown(EsRelation.class, esRelation -> {
                if (!hasScoring && esRelation.output()
                    .stream()
                    .anyMatch(a -> a instanceof MetadataAttribute && a.name().equals(MetadataAttribute.SCORE))) {
                    hasScoring = true;
                }
            });
        });
    }
    physicalPlan = physicalPlan.transformUp(FragmentExec.class, f -> {
        QueryBuilder fragmentFilter = f.esFilter();
        QueryBuilder newFilter;
        if (fragmentFilter != null) {
            newFilter = boolQuery().filter(fragmentFilter).clause(hasScoring ? Queries.Clause.MUST : Queries.Clause.FILTER, filter);
        } else {
            newFilter = hasScoring ? filter : boolQuery().filter(filter);
        }
        LOGGER.debug("Fold filter {} to EsQueryExec", newFilter);
        return f.withFilter(newFilter);
    });
}
```

